 ],
 "literal": "O relatives, may you live long, O relatives! Every day my / heart-binding took, she of the beautiful fine hair, / large-shouldered young woman's small, soft chest / one day to embrace, if I embrace, / half a day's life even, I do not desire, indeed.",
 "translation": "May you live long, my friends! If I could embrace, even for a single day, the small, soft chest of that young woman with large shoulders and beautiful, fine hair, who has bound my heart day after day, I would not desire to live even for half a day more.",
 "modern": "என் உறவினர்களே! நீங்கள் வாழ்க! நாள்தோறும் என் நெஞ்சைக் கட்டிப்போட்ட, அழகிய மென்மையான கூந்தலையும் பெரிய தோள்களையும் உடைய அந்த இளம்பெண்ணின் சிறிய மென்மையான மார்பை ஒருநாள் தழுவக் கூடுமானால், அதற்குப் பிறகு அரைநாள் கூட உயிர்வாழ நான் விரும்பமாட்டேன்.",
 "explanation": "The hero speaks to his friends or relatives who are advising him to restrain his intense passion. He declares that his heart has been completely captured and bound day after day by the young woman with beautiful fine hair and large shoulders. He asserts that if he could embrace her small, soft chest for just a single day, he would not wish to live even for half a day after that. This intense longing and desire for union are characteristic of the Kuriñci landscape. The key words are 'kēḷir' (friends/relatives), 'neñcu piṇi koṇṭa' (captured my heart), and 'araināḷ vāḻkkaiyum vēṇṭaleṉ' (I do not want even half a day's life).",
